Z||000000||Ted||10-28-1999||08:54 PM||||<BR>I have a '85 2m4 and it is standard. My clutch fluid is low and I don't have the manual and was wondering what fluid I could use for it?||||reg||1
Z||000001||Patrick||10-28-1999||09:08 PM||||<BR>You probably have <B>DOT3</B> brake fluid in there right now. However, if you've ever had any problems with your clutch hydraulic system, you might want to read this mega thread:<P> <A HREF="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum2/HTML/000034.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum2/HTML/000034.html</A> <P>Believe it or not, there are a few of us who have solved our problems by flushing out the DOT3 and using <B>ATF</B> (automatic transmission fluid) instead. Any and all details are in that thread. ||||reg||4
